  "description": "174 Harrow View",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 0cm 5.4pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:0cm 5.4pt; text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;It has not been demonstrated to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority that the use or operations described in the application would be lawful within the meaning of S192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) if instituted or begun at the time of the application. Specifically, the proposed use of the dwellinghouse as a residential care facility for local children with learning disabilities would result in a material change of use from Class C3 (Dwellinghouse) to Use Class C2 and would therefore not be within the tolerances of the Town and Country Planning (Use Class) Order 1987 (as amended). &lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:0cm 5.4pt; text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding:0cm 5.4pt; text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;The proposal is therefore not a lawful development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
